@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ Verification and password-reset mail is sent with Action Mailer. Set the Action
 - `POST /api/v1/password_resets` and `/confirm`: request/complete password reset.
 - `GET /api/v1/account`, `POST /api/v1/account/cancel`, `POST /api/v1/account/reactivate`: account lifecycle.
 
-Request, ticket, comment, user, staff, and invitation lists accept `page` and `per_page` (defaults: `1` and `25`) and return pagination metadata. Customer-facing conversation replies are stored in the portal and do not send email; staff can add private ticket notes with `comment.public: false`.
+Request, ticket, comment, user, staff, and invitation lists accept `page` and `per_page` (defaults: `1` and `25`) and return pagination metadata. Staff can set ticket `priority` to `normal` (the default) or `high`; ticket lists can combine `status`, `assignee_id` (including `unassigned`), `requester_id`, `priority`, and `q` filters. Search is case-insensitive across subjects and public comments. Customers can filter their own requests by `status`; priority is staff-only. Customer-facing conversation replies are stored in the portal and do not send email; staff can add private ticket notes with `comment.public: false`.
 
 Cancelled accounts can be permanently removed with `bin/rails helpdesk:purge_cancelled_accounts` after their 90-day reactivation window.
 
